Subject: Four-way named-read cache with a two-prototype entry, Array and rope-string receivers, and retained empty allocator arenas

What this does
  Four-way named-read cache with a two-prototype entry, Array and rope-string receivers, and retained empty allocator arenas.

Why we need it
  And what the allocator was doing. A read site held two shapes; 35,879 of them stub-cache hits. A site now has `REGVM_PIC_WAYS` = 4 ways, probed by `regvm_poly_read_hit` before the slow function, and a way that keeps hitting is promoted to the primary way, middle and holder shapes, all hashed and so immutable, and Array.prototype as a holder, were refused by the fill because Arrays are exotic, so every `arr.push` / `arr.join` read was a full lookup.

What it adds
  `REGVM_PIC_WAYS`, `REG_PIC_PROTO2`, `regvm_poly_read_hit`, `regvm_mega_read`, `regvm_get_field_ic_slow`, `JS_ARENA_EMPTY_MAX`, `JSArenaState.n_empty`, `js_arena_trim`; the PIC table is 4 entries per site and its holder array 8; test `tests/differential/corpus/read-cache-ways-and-receivers.js`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
